  "instagram_caption": "It's not a morning thing. It's a night shift 🌙\n\nHealthy men get up to five erections a night during REM sleep, each lasting 20 to 30 minutes. It isn't caused by dreams: in REM the nervous system switches to rest and digest, blood flow goes up, and you often wake up right out of the last one.\n\nScientists think the extra oxygen may help keep the tissue healthy. If they disappear for weeks, talk to a doctor.\n\nSources: University of Newcastle, The Conversation, PubMed, Ro.\n\nDid you know this happens while you sleep?\n\n#docstick #mensHealth #sleepscience #bodyfacts #sexeducation",
  "youtube_title": "Why Morning Wood Happens (It's a Night Shift)",
  "youtube_description": "Healthy men get up to five erections a night during REM sleep, each lasting 20 to 30 minutes. It isn't caused by dreams: REM switches the nervous system to rest and digest, and you often wake up right out of the last one. If they disappear for weeks, talk to a doctor.\n\nEducational only, not medical advice.\n\nSources:\n• University of Newcastle, \"Male erections\" (fetched Nov 26, 2026)\n• The Conversation via Inverse, \"What causes morning erections?\" (fetched Nov 26, 2026)\n• PubMed, \"Sleep-related erections: neural mechanisms and clinical significance\" (fetched Nov 26, 2026)\n• Ro, \"Morning wood\" (fetched Nov 26, 2026)\n\nDoc Stick: the stuff school skipped. Instagram: @askdocstick\n\n#MensHealth #SleepScience #Shorts"
